      "result": {
        "content": "Sure, here's a list of the tools I currently have access to and what they can do:\n\n- `get_datetime`: This tool returns the current date and time in ISO 8601 format (which is UTC by default), Unix timestamp, and human-readable format.\n  \n- `duckduckgo_search`: It allows you to search the web using DuckDuckGo. When the main 'web_search' tool isn't available, this becomes an alternative.\n\n- `web_search`: A powerful tool for performing multiple searches from Google and DuckDuckGo, summarizing key results, and providing deep context analysis.\n\n- `web_fetch`: This fetches the content of a public URL into a text format that can be read easily. It's useful when you need to examine specific web pages or articles.\n\n- `read_file`: Reads the contents of files within a sandbox environment. For security reasons, it must come with user confirmation and operates on allowed paths.\n\n- `smart_search`: This tool synthesizes various research sources including Wikipedia, internal memory, and web data into professional reports containing verified citations and deep context.\n\n- `shell_execute`: It allows you to execute shell commands inside a Docker container securely. For use in compiling code, system management tasks, or running scripts.\n\n- `list_dir`: Provides the list of files within a directory sandboxed environment, which can be useful for exploring file systems before reading them into memory.\n\n- `web-search` (modified version): This tool is capable of performing detailed web searches using DuckDuckGo and fetching relevant results like titles and URLs along with summaries.\n\n- `iask-search`: AI-powered search using IAsk.ai. It returns comprehensive, AI-generated responses based on web content. Available modes include \"question\" for general queries, \"academic\" for scholarly research, etc., with various detail levels.\n\n- `monica-search`: Another version of AI-powered search using Monica AI, providing insights into a wide array of results and question types, including detailed information.\n\nPlease note that some tools may not be available or working as expected under certain circumstances. This list is always under development to ensure it meets the latest requirements and specifications.Is there something specific you'd like help with today?",
